  "notes": "Higher weight = query first / trust faster. Cap 20. Min 1. Sweep on 2026-05-27 added 6 new sources, reweighted 4 existing, 2 new advisories. New advisories: (1) 2026-05-composio-ai-agent-platform-breach — Composio AI-agent infrastructure platform breached 2026-05-21 (01:05–09:15 PT), disclosed 2026-05-22. Attacker brute-forced exploit chains with **LLM-generated attack patterns**, gained foothold in an internal monitoring agent, pivoted to automated remediation, then **registered malicious tool definitions inside the sandboxed execution environment** to reach arbitrary code execution; reached an auxiliary cache holding ~5,241 customer API keys + ~5,001 user GitHub OAuth connections (~0.3% of active). Internal lateral via compromised Gmail OAuth tokens of Composio employees + magic-link sign-in. Composio revoked all GitHub tokens, mandated rotation of all dev API keys by 2026-05-23 23:00 PT, deleted every API key created before 2026-05-22 23:00 PT. Second documented 'AI tool → cloud platform' OAuth pivot (after Vercel/Context.ai), and first with attacker openly using LLM-augmented exploitation + a *malicious-tool-definition-in-sandbox* primitive — the agent-platform analogue of MCP tool poisoning. (2) 2026-05-cargo-symlink-sparse-url-cves — first Cargo-itself CVEs in this repo, disclosed by Rust Security Response Team 2026-05-25, both fixed in Rust 1.96.0 (2026-05-28): **CVE-2026-5223** (medium) — Cargo did not reject symlinks inside crate tarballs from third-party registries → malicious crate's tarball extracts one directory up and overwrites the cached source of another crate from the same registry; **crates.io itself NOT affected** because it rejects symlink uploads server-side, but corporate/mirror registries that don't are. **CVE-2026-5222** (low) — sparse-registry URL normalization unintentionally strips `.git` suffix, replaying creds for `…/index.git` against `…/index`. Folded Crates.io/Rust into 'registry-side hygiene matters' theme; first generalization of [TrapDoor](advisories/2026-05-trapdoor-cross-ecosystem-stealer.md)'s Rust arm into Cargo-level CVE coverage. Skill updates applied: added 'agent-platform-as-MCP-broker' (Composio class) as a recurring named-instance pattern in the Tier-B vendor rotation (sibling of 'cloud-provider MCP' added 2026-05-26); added 'LLM-augmented attacker' as a triage cue — when a vendor IR post describes 'exceptional speed / deep knowledge of internal architecture,' note explicit AI-augmentation if disclosed; added 'malicious-tool-definition-in-sandbox' as a *write-target* surface alongside `.cursorrules`/`CLAUDE.md`/`SKILL.md`/`AGENTS.md` (registration of new tools/skills/connectors is a privileged write, not a documentation annotation). Prior sweep (2026-05-26) added 4 new sources, reweighted 8 existing, 1 new advisory (Shai-Hulud 3.0 backfill) + 1 update (systemic MCP advisory). New advisory: (1) 2025-12-shai-hulud-3-test-payload — @vietmoney/react-big-calendar@0.26.2 carrying a heavily-obfuscated Shai-Hulud v3 ('Holiday Whisper'/Snyk; 'Shai-Hulud 3.0'/Upwind+Mondoo+OX) dropped 2025-12-28; low spread (Aikido: 'caught attackers testing payload'), but in retrospect the TeamPCP rehearsal for the SAP -> PyTorch Lightning -> Bitwarden 'Third Coming' -> TanStack/Mistral -> @antv+durabletask wave that followed in April-May 2026. Backfilled to close the v1->v2->v3 lineage gap. Update: 2026-05-mcp-stdio-systemic-rce -- folded in two new named instances: (a) aws-mcp-server CVE-2026-5058 + CVE-2026-5059 (CVSS 9.8 each; unauthenticated command-injection RCE in the allowed-commands list handler; ZDI-26-245/-246; patches pending at disclosure 2026-04-11 -- treat as unfixed-in-the-wild; this is the community/third-party 'aws-mcp-server', NOT AWS's official 'AWS API MCP' which has its own CVE-2026-4270 file-access bypass); (b) n8n-mcp CVE-2026-39974 (post-auth SSRF in multi-tenant HTTP mode: server reflects URL response bodies back via JSON-RPC, attacker reads cloud IMDS for temp creds; affects <=2.47.3, fixed 2.47.4). Skill updates applied: (1) extended the 'AI-agent config files are a write-target' caution to include SKILL.md and reference the Cloud Security Alliance 'Agent Context Poisoning' research note (2026-05-06) which formally names this attack surface; (2) added 'cloud-provider MCP' as a named-instance pattern in the Tier-B vendor rotation and clarified that community 'aws-mcp-server' vs AWS's official 'AWS API MCP' are distinct CVE streams. Deferred: CSA SKILL.md research note itself (research/analysis, not an incident; covered by the skill caution update); n8n core RCE CVE-2025-68613 (out of window, 2025); LiteSpeed CVE-2026-48172 + Drupal CVE-2026-9082 (not vibe-coding-relevant); Moltbook 1.5M API keys (already in ongoing-vibe-platform-exposure). Prior sweep (2026-05-25) added 4 new sources, reweighted 5 existing, 1 new advisory + 1 update. New advisory: (1) 2026-05-trapdoor-cross-ecosystem-stealer — Socket-flagged 'TrapDoor': 34+ malicious packages / 384+ versions pushed to npm + PyPI + Crates.io at once (first activity 2026-05-22 20:20 UTC), impersonating crypto/DeFi/AI/security dev tooling (prompt-engineering-toolkit, solidity-deploy-guard, defi-threat-scanner). npm postinstall -> trap-core.js (~1,149-line harvester, live-validates AWS/GitHub tokens); PyPI auto-exec on import; Rust build.rs -> XOR-encrypt keystores -> GitHub Gists. New pattern: supply-chain package WRITES zero-width-Unicode prompt injection into .cursorrules / CLAUDE.md so the dev's own AI agent re-exfiltrates secrets under guise of an 'automated security scan' (AI-config-as-persistence/re-infection; inverts the earlier read-only AI-config theft of Bitwarden CLI / Nx Console). Markers: GitHub ddjidd564, ddjidd564.github.io, P-2024-001. Distinct actor (not TeamPCP). Adds Crates.io/Rust (build.rs) to the cross-ecosystem rotation. Update: 2026-05-mcp-stdio-systemic-rce — folded in @mcpjam/inspector CVE-2026-23744 (binds 0.0.0.0, no auth, zero-interaction RCE installing a malicious MCP server; <=1.4.2, fixed 1.4.3) as another 'MCP surface trusted-by-default' named instance. Skill updates applied: added Crates.io + AI-config-poisoning Tier-A queries; broadened cross-ecosystem-worm caution to npm/PyPI/Crates (build.rs); added an 'AI-agent config files are a write-target' caution bullet. Prior sweep (2026-05-24) added 3 new sources, reweighted 8 existing, 1 new advisory + 1 update. New advisory: (1) 2026-05-shai-hulud-copycat-wave — after TeamPCP open-sourced the Mini Shai-Hulud worm (2026-05-12) and posted a $1,000 BreachForums 'biggest supply-chain attack' competition, low-skill copycats shipped near-verbatim clones on npm. Actor deadcode09284814 published 4 packages (~2,700 dl): chalk-tempalte (worm clone, C2 87e0bbc636999b.lhr.life), @deadcode09284814/axios-util (cred exfil -> 80.200.28.28:2222), axois-utils (Golang 'Phantom Bot' DDoS + Win/Linux persistence), color-style-utils (IP/geo/wallet -> edcf8b03c84634.lhr.life). New pattern: worm-source-goes-public + paid attack competition -> commoditized copycat wave with diversified payloads (DDoS, not just stealers); *.lhr.life (localhost.run SSH tunnel) as disposable C2. Update: 2026-02-clawhavoc-clawhub-skills — added Snyk 'ToxicSkills' ecosystem audit (3,984 skills across ClawHub + skills.sh; prompt injection in 36%; 1,467 malicious payloads; 2.9% fetch-and-execute remote content at runtime so scan-on-publish misses them; 'skill scanner = false security'). Prior-sweep context (2026-05-23): added Bitwarden CLI AI-tool-cred-hunting backdoor, elementary-data .pth+GHCR compromise, Marimo pre-auth RCE, OpenVSX recommended-extension hijack, Cursor/Windsurf stale-Chromium n-days. New advisories: (1) Bitwarden CLI @bitwarden/cli 2026.4.0 backdoor — TeamPCP 'Shai-Hulud: The Third Coming' Checkmarx-channel campaign; first supply-chain malware with a module that specifically hunts AI-coding-tool creds + MCP files (Claude Code/Cursor/Codex); (2) elementary-data 0.23.3 PyPI+GHCR compromise — malicious .pth auto-exec on every Python startup, GitHub Actions script injection -> forged signed release -> real publish pipeline, 1M+/mo downloads, fixed 0.23.4; (3) Marimo notebook pre-auth RCE CVE-2026-39987 — unauth /terminal/ws WebSocket -> PTY shell, exploited 9h41m post-disclosure (Sysdig), CISA KEV, fixed 0.23.0; (4) VS Code fork OpenVSX recommended-extension namespace hijack (Koi) — Cursor/Windsurf/Antigravity/Trae recommend non-existent extensions, namespaces unclaimed -> install malware via the IDE's own 'Recommended' prompt; Cursor fixed 12/1, Google 1/1, Windsurf no response; (5) Cursor & Windsurf stale-Chromium 94+ n-days (OX 'Forked and Forgotten') — CVE-2025-7656 weaponized vs latest builds, 1.8M devs, vendor-dismissed. Updates: systemic MCP stdio class (+network-ai CVE-2026-46701 empty-default-secret), TanStack/Mini Shai-Hulud (campaign timeline extended to the April Bitwarden/Checkmarx arm + elementary-data TTP cross-link; UNC6780=Google tracker), Cursor open-folder (cross-linked the two new Cursor-surface advisories). New patterns this run: (a) supply-chain malware now treats authenticated AI coding tools (config + MCP files) as a first-class credential objective — Bitwarden CLI is the first documented case; (b) .pth-file-as-execution-primitive (auto-exec at Python interpreter startup) + lockstep GHCR Docker-image poisoning; (c) recommendation-poisoning via marketplace divergence (IDE recommends MS-Marketplace names but installs from OpenVSX where the namespace is unclaimed) — slopsquatting-adjacent but distinct; (d) AI/data tools shipping unauthenticated network endpoints (Marimo joins Langflow/PraisonAI) -> sub-day disclosure-to-exploit; (e) stale-Chromium n-day exposure as a standing class in Electron-based AI IDEs.",
